.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 3, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-BUILD-AETHER-BASELINE 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-build-aether-baseline
.Nd build and optionally boot a pinned offline Aether developer baseline
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3 scripts/build-aether-baseline.py
.Ar output
.Fl Fl dependencies Ar directory
.Op Fl Fl tools Ar paths.json
.Op Fl Fl supervised
.Op Fl Fl service-table
.Op Fl Fl smoke
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Run from the source repository root using the recorded macOS arm64 tools.
The output must be fresh below out/ with an existing parent and no symlink or
parent-traversal components. Inputs and tool executable hashes are checked before
staging. This command does not fetch, install or modify sibling repositories.
.Fl Fl smoke
boots one useful bytecount cycle and halt in a private QEMU guest.
The startup test probe takes about 30 seconds.
.Fl Fl service-table
selects the qualified static three-role policy without the startup test probe.
The default preserves the old baseline; table-only automatic retries remain zero.
.Fl Fl supervised
requires --service-table and selects one pre-effect command replacement after
known cleanup. Failure after I/O or exhausted retry closes admission. This policy
applies only to the frozen mediated bytecount workload.
.Fl Fl tools
relocates identical executables; it cannot change their locked hashes.
.Sh OUTPUT
Progress uses stderr. Success JSON uses stdout.
The output retains result.json, phase logs, image hashes and, when requested,
serial.log, qemu.log and smoke.json. Failures retain owned output; use a new output
for a subsequent attempt.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 operational failure; 2 blocked precondition; 64 invalid usage;
130 keyboard interruption. Help and version exit 0 on stdout.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/build-aether-baseline.py out/my-baseline \\
  --dependencies out/si07-loop/.deps --smoke
.Ed
.Sh LIMITATIONS
This is a developer ABI22 fixed-memory workload, not an installed product,
interactive shell or authenticated console. Developer r/h input runs one cycle
or halts between cycles. Build-only success is not target acceptance. Tool bounds
are 180 seconds and 4 MiB per phase; the guest bounds are 90 seconds and 4 MiB.
No host sandbox or complete shared-library closure is claimed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
docs/AETHER-BASELINE.md, docs/SI07-DISPOSITION.md,
docs/aether-baseline.lock.json
